frac23xe^{3x}-\\frac29e^{3x}$. Hence\n$$\\int_0^{1/3}2xe^{3x}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac23xe^{3x}-\\frac29e^{3x}\\right]_0^{1/3}\n=0-\\left(-\\frac29\\right)=\\frac29.$$" 13194139534607 false] [17592186298506 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298507 13194139534607 true] [17592186298506 1089 "q-114289" 13194139534607 true] [17592186298506 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534607 true] [17592186298506 1100 "Calculate $\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534607 true] [17592186298506 1113 #uuid "28cbd3f2-ea47-530d-8403-83a96b31400a" 13194139534607 true] [17592186298506 1145 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{3}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & ={3}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{3}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534607 true] [17592186298507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298508 13194139534607 true] [17592186298507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298509 13194139534607 true] [17592186298507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298510 13194139534607 true] [17592186298507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298511 13194139534607 true] [17592186298507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298